LAME 3.100: remove lame_init_old from the export list of libmp3lame.

include/libmp3lame.sym exports lame_init_old, which LAME 3.100 no longer defines, and the macOS
linker rejects an exported symbol that is not defined in a shared library. Homebrew and MacPorts
drop the line the same way. No source code changes.

Sonara's scripts/native/build-codecs.sh applies this patch to the official lame-3.100.tar.gz
before it configures LAME. To apply it by hand, in the extracted lame-3.100 folder:

    patch -p1 < lame-3.100-export-list.patch

--- a/include/libmp3lame.sym
+++ b/include/libmp3lame.sym
@@ -1,5 +1,4 @@
 lame_init
-lame_init_old
 lame_set_num_samples
 lame_get_num_samples
 lame_set_in_samplerate
